          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Sometimes in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
            one considers objects equipped with two different types of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extra+structure"} extra structure
            which interact in a suitable way. For instance, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            equipped with both (1) the structure of an (additive)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            and (2) the structure of a (multiplicative)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo +
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi a
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi b
                  %mo +
                  %mi a
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\cdot (b+c) = a\cdot b + a\cdot c
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\cdot 0 = 0
          %p
            Abstractly, there are two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads"} monads
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+a+monad"} algebras
            are abelian groups, and one (call it
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+object"} free
            ring on that set, which consists of formal sums of formal products of elements of
            = succeed "\u2014in" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(S(X))
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T S
            into a monad?”
          %p
            It is easy to give
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T S
            a unit, as the composite
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Id
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi η
                          %mi S
                    %mi S
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi η
                          %mi T
                        %mi S
                    %mi T
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id \xrightarrow{\eta^S} S \xrightarrow{\eta^T S} T S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi S
                  %mi T
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T S T S
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi μ
                    %mi T
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi T
                  %mi T
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu^T\colon T T \to T
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi μ
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi S
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu^S\colon S S \to S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi S
                    %mi T
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda\colon S T \to T S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi μ
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu^{T S}
            to be the composite
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi S
                    %mi T
                    %mi S
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi λ
                    %mi T
                    %mi T
                    %mi S
                    %mi S
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi μ
                          %mi T
                        %msup
                          %mi μ
                          %mi S
                    %mi T
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T S T S \xrightarrow{\lambda} T T S S \xrightarrow{\mu^T\mu^S} T S
          %p
            Such a transformation
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi S
                    %mi T
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda\colon S T \to T S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T S
            into a monad, is called a
            = succeed "," do
              %em distributive law
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S T X
            is a formal product of formal sums such as
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 4
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 5
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x_1 + x_2 + x_3)\cdot (x_4 + x_5)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            is given by multiplying out such an expression formally, resulting in a formal sum of formal products such as
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 4
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 5
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 4
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 5
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 3
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 4
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 3
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 5
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1\cdot x_4 + x_1 \cdot x_5 + x_2 \cdot x_4 + x_2 \cdot x_5 + x_3\cdot x_4 + x_3 \cdot x_5
          %p
            Given two monads
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S, T
            on a category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi T
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi T
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \circ T \longrightarrow T \circ S
            gives a way of lifting the monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to a monad on the category of
            = succeed "-algebras," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Moore+category"} Eilenberg-Moore category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            for abelian groups (which is a monad on
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo =
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = Set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi S
                    %mo =
                    %mi Mon
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^S = Mon
          %p
          #TerminologyWhatDistributesOverWhat.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (terminology – what distributes over what)
              %br/
              The eponymous example of distributivity in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic"} arithmetic
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ×
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi i
                    %mi a
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    a \times \sum_i b_i \;=\; \sum_i a \times b_i
            %p hence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\big( a \times (-) \big)
                    \\circ
                    \\big(
                    \\sum (-)
                    \\big)
                    \\;\;
                    \=
                    \\;\;
                    \\big(
                    \\sum (-)
                    \\big)
                    \\circ
                    \\big( a \times (-) \big)
            %p
              (where, of course, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equality
              as such works in both directions, but the
              %em distribution
              of factors over summands is the step from left to right) suggests that a suitable transformation of (co)monads of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi T
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi T
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S \circ T \longrightarrow T \circ S
            %p
              should be referred to as
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                distributing over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              instead of the other way around.
            %p
              However, already the original reference
              %a{:href => "#Beck69"} Beck 1969 §1
              uses the opposite terminology.
            %p
              Authors sticking to this original but arguably reverse terminological convention include
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#BrookesVanStone93"} Brookes &amp; Van Stone 1993
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#BarrWells85"} Barr &amp; Wells 1985 §9 2.1
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#PowerWatanabe02"} Power &amp; Watanabe 2002 p. 138
          %h2#BigPicture Big picture
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} Monads
            in any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            make themselves a 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Mnd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Mnd}
            in which
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-morphisms"} 1-morphisms
            are either lax or colax
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
            of monads (cf.
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad+transformations"} monad transformations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duality"} formal duality
            the analogue is true for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonads"} comonads
          %p
            Distributivity laws may be understood as monads
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
            to this 2-category of monads.
          %p In particular, distributive laws themselves make a 2-category.
          %p
            There are other variants like distributive laws between a monad and an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctor"} endofunctor
            %strong mixed distributive laws
            between a monad and a comonad (the variants for algebras and coalgebras called
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entwining+structures"} entwining structures
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PROP"} PROP
          %p
            Having a distributive law
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi l
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l
            from one monad to another enables one to define the composite monad
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi T
                    %msub
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi l
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf T\circ_l\mathbf P
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} comp
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Mnd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Mnd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
