              %g{:fill => "rgb(0%, 0%, 0%)", "fill-opacity" => "1"}
                %use{:x => "124.157", "xlink:href" => "#lIqpFp2fS2V4Xvqh6euvCdP074M=-glyph-1-3", :y => "73.427"}
            %p
          (due to
          = succeed "," do
            %a{:href => "#Beck69"} Beck 1969
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "#BarrWells85"} Barr &amp; Wells 1985 §9 2.1
          %p
            The correspondence between distributive laws and
            %em endofunctor
            liftings extends to a correspondence between distributive laws and
            %em monad
            liftings. That is, distributive laws
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi l
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi T
                  %mi P
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi P
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l \colon T P \Rightarrow P T
            from the monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{T}
            to the monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{P}
            are in a canonical bijection with lifts of the monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{P}
            to a monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi P
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{P}^{\mathbf T}
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Moore+category"} Eilenberg-Moore category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{\mathbf T}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi U
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi T
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi T
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^{\mathbf T} \colon A^{\mathbf T}\to A
            preserves the monad structure.
          %p
            Thus all together a distributive law for a monad over a monad is a 2-cell for which 2 triangles and 2 pentagons commute. In the entwining case, Brzeziński and Majid combined the 4 diagrams into one picture which they call the
            = succeed "." do
              %em bow-tie diagram
          %p
          #DistributivityAsMonadsInMonads.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (distributivity as monads in monads)
              %br/
              As mentioned earlier, one can understand a distributivity law of a monad
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,s)
              over another monad
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,t)
              as displaying
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi a
                    %mo →
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \colon a \to a
              as a monad on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,t)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} in
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Mnd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Mnd}(A)
              of monads in a 2-category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %p
              Specifically, a monad in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Mnd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Mnd}(A)
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,t)
              (which is a monad in
              = succeed "!)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  A
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-morphism"} 1-morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi a
