              satisfy correspond to those of a distributive law.
          %h3#monad_distributing_over_a_comonad Monad distributing over a comonad
          %p
            %a{:href => "#vanOsdol73"} van Osdol 1973 p. 456
          %p (…)
          %h3#ComonadDistributingOverMonad Comonad distributing over monad
          %p The distributivity law of
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a comonad
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                over
            %li
              %p
                a monad
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
          %p
            on the same
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
          %p
            is as follows (
            %a{:href => "#BrookesVanStone93"}> Brookes &amp; Van Stone 1993 Def. 3
            ,
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#PowerWatanabe02"} Power &amp; Watanabe 2002
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi distr
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mtext -
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℰ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  distr^{\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{E}}_{(\text{-})}
                  \\;\;\colon\;\;
                  \\mathcal{C}
                  \\big(
                  \\mathcal{E}(-)
                  \\big)
                  \\longrightarrow
                  \\mathcal{E}
                  \\big(
                  \\mathcal{C}(-)
                  \\big)
          %p
            such that the following
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} diagrams commute
            for all objects
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
          %div{:style => "margin: -20px 0px 20px 0px"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/MixedCoMonadDistributivity-230929.jpg", :width => "540px"}/
          %p#TwoSidedKleisliComposition
            Given this distributivity structure, there is a two-sided (“double”)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+category"} Kleisli category
            (
            %a{:href => "#BrookesVanStone93"}> Brookes &amp; Van Stone 1993 Thm. 2
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#PowerWatanabe02"} Power &amp; Watanabe 2002, Prop. 7.4
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            are those of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_1 \to D_2
            are morphisms in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi prog
                    %mn 12
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  prog_{12}
                  \\;\colon\;
                  \\mathcal{C}(D_1)
                  \\longrightarrow
                  \\mathcal{E}(D_2)
          %p with two-sided Kleisli composition
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi prog
                    %mn 12
                  %mtext &gt;=&gt;
                  %msub
                    %mi prog
                    %mn 23
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  prog_{12} \text{&gt;=&gt;} prog_{23}
                  \\;\;
                  \\colon
                  \\;\;
                  \\mathcal{C}(D_1)
                  \\longrightarrow
                  \\mathcal{E}(D_3)
          %p
            given by the (co-)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+extension"} bind-operation
            on the factors connected by the distributivity transformation:
          %div{:style => "margin: -20px 0px 20px 0px"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/CoMonKleisliComposition-230930b.pdf", :width => "800px"}/
          %h2#algebras_for_a_distributive_law Algebras for a distributive law
          %p
            Given a composite monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T S
            arising from a distributive law
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi l
                    %mo :
                    %mi S
                    %mi T
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi T
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l : S T \Rightarrow T S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T S
            comprises an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            with both
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s : S A \to A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t : T A \to A
